;; ============================================================================
;;
;;   quotes.wat :: a quote-of-the-day engine, hand-written in WebAssembly Text
;;
;; ============================================================================
;;
;;   This file is GENERATED by `python -m tools.qotd wat`. Edit the fragments
;;   in src/wat/ or the seeds in database/ instead, then rebuild.
;;
;;   The module has no imports. Everything the page needs (calendar math, the
;;   pseudo-random schedule, and every quote with its author) lives in its
;;   linear memory and is reached through a handful of exports:
;;
;;     quote_for_date(y, m, d) -> i32     index of the quote for a civil date
;;     quote_text_ptr/len(i)   -> i32     UTF-8 (ASCII) bytes of the quote
;;     quote_author_ptr/len(i) -> i32     UTF-8 (ASCII) bytes of the author
;;
;;   The embedded schedule covers one full Gregorian cycle (146097 days,
;;   2000-01-01 .. 2399-12-31). Outside it, the same schedule is recomputed
;;   on the fly with PCG32 and a Fisher-Yates shuffle.
;;
